# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Conventional Commits. A scope is required (house rule); never omit it.
# Allowed types:
#   feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, ci, build, revert
# Scope: the module or area touched. For this repo:
#   money, events, ledger, auth, fees, interest, replay, report
# For cross-cutting work use: repo, deps, docs, config.
#
# Examples:
#   feat(fees): assess one overdraft fee per account per day
#   fix(interest): sum the rounded daily accruals rather than rounding the sum
#   docs(readme): explain why the suite reports one failure
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no trailing period; header under 100 chars.
# Body (optional): leave a blank line, then explain what changed and why; wrap at 100.
# Footer (optional): BREAKING CHANGE: <description>, or Refs: <id>.
